index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..73e9ff1b7f92137f0836c905379016849b967fc3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/native-runtime/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+# Independent native CPU foundation
+
+Configure from this directory, without the suyu root build graph. The current target is a synthetic Stage A/B verification host, not an MK8-capable platform.
+
+Run from any directory:
+
+```
+python G:/suyu/mk8-native-runtime/source/tests/native_platform/run.py --build G:/suyu/mk8-native-runtime/native-platform/build
+```
+
+Existing Python, CMake, C11 and C++20 are sufficient. No downloaded dependencies, keys, firmware or game assets are required. The runner bootstraps the existing emitter, generates two synthetic modules plus the existing synthetic extracted NSO fixture, then links the emitted static module projects and one shared C runtime. It uses hosted SVC/barrier/unhandled semantics without linking Core, HLE or Dynarmic targets. MSVC builds use the static CRT; dependency and symbol-map checks reject host/graphics/JIT imports.
+
+`Host` owns one guest context, a fixed 256KiB callback memory bus, a deterministic virtual counter, a shared reservation monitor and bounded cross-module slices. Read/write/execute permissions and scalar access ordering are explicit. Fastmem and the ABI5 page-table walk remain disabled: callbacks must stay authoritative until native mapping/store invalidation is integrated. Interrupts are checked before each bounded slice. This is a deterministic single-thread scheduler, with no claim of concurrent guest scheduling.
+
+The supported SVC subset includes memory queries, owned-process layout/accounting and entropy queries, current-thread metadata, counter reads, bounded nonnegative sleep, debug output, process exit, and native session connect/send/close. The process capability list gates dispatch. Synthetic sleep advances a virtual 19.2MHz counter; the optional actual CPU diagnostic uses a steady host counter and native positive sleep. Thread waits and scheduling remain unsupported. SignalProcessWideKey supports the verified empty-waiter case only. Unsupported SVCs, unknown module PCs/imports, unsupported opcodes, breakpoints in normal dispatch, permission failures and exhausted execution bounds are fatal errors. No path returns a fabricated service success.
+
+`load_synthetic` supports the exact uncompressed three-page NSO shape produced by the existing export integration fixture. It pins complete text bytes to the compiled static image, checks NPDM process/capability bounds, and reads the fixture's single RomFS file with checked extents. This is deliberately a restricted synthetic loader, not a production NSO/NPDM/RomFS implementation or signature verifier. Malformed and unsupported shapes fail before guest execution.
+
+Tests cover full-context canaries, module transitions, slice budgets 1/3/4096, memory traces, counter/SVC stops, virtual sleep and exit, generated exclusive/barrier instructions, reservation invalidation, code/data protection, interrupts, original code guards with generation invalidation, and seven malformed loader cases. The fixture must emit its exact debug marker, sleep 100ms in virtual time, read exact RomFS content and exit cleanly.
+
+Not implemented here: concurrent application threading/waits, general kernel objects, application service endpoints, save writes, audio/input, graphics, general content filesystems and full title startup. The native SM router supports owned sessions and initialization; the LM endpoint creates owned logger sessions and delivers bounded packets to an explicitly configured native file sink. Missing endpoints fail with a named diagnostic. Protocol close releases the endpoint while retaining its client kernel handle until CloseHandle. Those boundaries remain explicit migration work; they cannot be satisfied by this harness's successful synthetic boot.
+
+## General NSO and sparse-address-space boundary
+
+`nso.h` exposes `load_nso`, `map_nso` and `relocate_rtld`; `address_space.h` owns sparse 39-bit regions. `Host.address_space` can route the unchanged RecompHostMem callbacks to this bus. GuestContext/RecompHostMem layouts are unchanged.
+
+The general NSO loader is separate from the restricted `load_synthetic` integration fixture. It supports nonempty text/rodata/data segments, page-aligned segment placement, bounded file/image sizes, BSS zero-fill, raw or LZ4-compressed segments, and advertised segment SHA256 checks. LZ4 comes from an explicitly supplied existing static library (`NATIVE_LZ4_LIBRARY`); no package is downloaded. Windows SHA256 uses the OS BCrypt backend. Other hosts reject hashed inputs until a native hash backend is supplied.
+
+Sparse mappings allocate backing only for mapped segments, enforce read/write/execute permissions, and reject overlap, overflow and unmapped access. Fastmem remains disabled. Relocation indexes checked dynamic symbol/string extents across modules, plans only rtld RELA writes, rejects unresolved strong/unsupported imports before writes, resolves undefined weak symbols to architectural zero, and zeroes only rtld's relocation-size fields. Relocation targets cannot escape rtld. The original two-argument relocation API remains available; an optional audit overload exposes exact slot values and weak-null classification.
+
+`native_loader_test` adds compressed/hash-failure fixtures, BSS/high-address mappings, scalar page boundaries, failed-write atomicity, malformed extents, weak/strong import behavior, unsupported relocation rejection and untouched non-rtld state. `native_admit EXEFS` reads and verifies four extracted modules, maps them from 0x80000000 using page-aligned image sizes, and pre-relocates rtld without executing guest instructions. Its output is admission evidence, not a boot or gameplay claim. NPDM/application-service/content-filesystem migration remains separate.
+
+## Optional actual static CPU diagnostic
+
+`run_boot.py` accepts private authenticated guest archives, their matching shared runtime, extracted ExeFS and an existing LZ4 library. It verifies identities, links a standalone CPU executable and records a bounded execution stop with registers and dependency evidence. These game-derived inputs and the resulting executable are private and must not be included in portable synthetic releases. The runner supplies a fresh exclusive-create diagnostic LM sink and records its hash, actual SVC/IPC trace and source/artifact hashes. An unsupported stop demonstrates only the executed CPU path, not title startup.
+
+Sparse reservations describe alias, heap, stack and TLS address ranges independently from committed backing. An enforced native physical-memory budget governs allocations. Executable regions are privately owned and sealed after mapping and rtld relocation: executable writes, overlapping maps and new executable mappings then fail. First block entry verifies original bytes; subsequent entries use the stable generation cache. No executable remap, alias or protection-change API is exposed. Changing that contract requires revoking cached guards before mutation.
diff --git a/native-runtime/address_space.cpp b/native-runtime/address_space.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..6018c3f0c44dc4925d6bcae758bbcbead83e17f1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/native-runtime/address_space.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,149 @@
+#include "address_space.h"
+#include <algorithm>
+#include <limits>
+#include <stdexcept>
+namespace native {
+bool AddressSpace::can_map(uint64_t address, uint64_t size,
+                           uint32_t state) const {
+  if (!size || address % 4096 || size % 4096 || address >= limit_ ||
+      size > limit_ - address)
+    return false;
+  auto next = regions_.lower_bound(address);
+  if (next != regions_.end() && next->first - address < size)
+    return false;
+  if (next != regions_.begin()) {
+    auto previous = std::prev(next);
+    if (address - previous->first < previous->second.bytes.size())
+      return false;
+  }
+  for (const auto &[_, reservation] : reservations_)
+    if (address < reservation.address + reservation.size &&
+        reservation.address < address + size) {
+      if (state != reservation.state || address < reservation.address ||
+          size > reservation.address + reservation.size - address)
+        return false;
+    }
+  return true;
+}
+void AddressSpace::reserve(uint64_t address, uint64_t size, uint32_t state) {
+  if ((state != 5 && state != 7 && state != 11 && state != 12) ||
+      !can_map(address, size))
+    throw std::runtime_error("virtual reservation range/state/overlap");
+  reservations_.emplace(address, MemoryRegionInfo{address, size, state, 0});
+}
+MemoryRegionInfo AddressSpace::reserved_range(uint32_t state) const {
+  const MemoryRegionInfo *found = nullptr;
+  for (const auto &[_, range] : reservations_)
+    if (range.state == state) {
+      if (found)
+        throw std::runtime_error("ambiguous virtual reservation");
+      found = &range;
+    }
+  if (!found)
+    throw std::runtime_error("missing native virtual reservation");
+  return *found;
+}
+void AddressSpace::map(uint64_t address, const std::vector<uint8_t> &bytes,
+                       uint64_t memory_size, unsigned permission,
+                       uint32_t state) {
+  if (code_sealed_ && (permission & 4))
+    throw std::runtime_error("executable mapping forbidden after code seal");
+  if ((permission != 1 && permission != 3 && permission != 5) ||
+      bytes.size() > memory_size ||
+      memory_size > std::numeric_limits<size_t>::max() ||
+      !can_map(address, memory_size, state))
+    throw std::runtime_error("sparse map range/overlap/permission");
+  if (state != 3 && state != 4 && state != 5 && state != 11 && state != 12)
+    throw std::runtime_error("unsupported memory region state");
+  if (memory_size > physical_budget_ - committed_bytes())
+    throw std::runtime_error("native process physical budget exhausted");
+  Region entry{address, std::vector<uint8_t>(size_t(memory_size)), permission,
+               state};
+  std::copy(bytes.begin(), bytes.end(), entry.bytes.begin());
+  regions_.emplace(address, std::move(entry));
+}
+const AddressSpace::Region &AddressSpace::region(uint64_t address,
+                                                 unsigned permission) const {
+  if (address >= limit_)
+    throw std::runtime_error("sparse address limit");
+  auto it = regions_.upper_bound(address);
+  if (it == regions_.begin())
+    throw std::runtime_error("sparse unmapped address");
+  --it;
+  if (address - it->first >= it->second.bytes.size() ||
+      (it->second.permission & permission) != permission)
+    throw std::runtime_error("sparse mapping permission");
+  return it->second;
+}
+uint64_t AddressSpace::read(uint64_t address, unsigned size,
+                            bool instruction) const {
+  if (!size || size > 8 || address >= limit_ || size > limit_ - address)
+    throw std::runtime_error("sparse read range");
+  uint64_t value = 0;
+  for (unsigned i = 0; i < size; ++i) {
+    const auto &r = region(address + i, instruction ? 4 : 1);
+    value |= uint64_t(r.bytes[size_t(address + i - r.address)]) << (8 * i);
+  }
+  return value;
+}
+void AddressSpace::write(uint64_t address, unsigned size, uint64_t value) {
+  if (!size || size > 8 || address >= limit_ || size > limit_ - address)
+    throw std::runtime_error("sparse write range");
+  for (unsigned i = 0; i < size; ++i)
+    (void)region(address + i, 2);
+  for (unsigned i = 0; i < size; ++i) {
+    auto &r = const_cast<Region &>(region(address + i, 2));
+    r.bytes[size_t(address + i - r.address)] = uint8_t(value >> (8 * i));
+  }
+}
+void AddressSpace::check(uint64_t address, unsigned size,
+                         unsigned permission) const {
+  if (!size || size > 8 || address >= limit_ || size > limit_ - address)
+    throw std::runtime_error("sparse check range");
+  for (unsigned i = 0; i < size; ++i)
+    (void)region(address + i, permission);
+}
+uint64_t AddressSpace::committed_bytes() const {
+  uint64_t total = 0;
+  for (const auto &[_, r] : regions_)
+    total += r.bytes.size();
+  return total;
+}
+MemoryRegionInfo AddressSpace::query(uint64_t address) const {
+  if (address >= limit_)
+    return {limit_, 0 - limit_, 16, 0};
+  auto next = regions_.upper_bound(address);
+  if (next != regions_.begin()) {
+    auto current = std::prev(next);
+    const auto &entry = current->second;
+    if (address - current->first < entry.bytes.size()) {
+      auto first = current, last = current;
+      while (first != regions_.begin()) {
+        auto prior = std::prev(first);
+        if (prior->first + prior->second.bytes.size() != first->first ||
+            prior->second.permission != entry.permission ||
+            prior->second.state != entry.state)
+          break;
+        first = prior;
+      }
+      while (std::next(last) != regions_.end()) {
+        auto following = std::next(last);
+        if (last->first + last->second.bytes.size() != following->first ||
+            following->second.permission != entry.permission ||
+            following->second.state != entry.state)
+          break;
+        last = following;
+      }
+      return {first->first,
+              last->first + last->second.bytes.size() - first->first,
+              entry.state, entry.permission};
+    }
+  }
+  const auto start =
+      next == regions_.begin()
+          ? 0
+          : std::prev(next)->first + std::prev(next)->second.bytes.size();
+  const auto end = next == regions_.end() ? limit_ : next->first;
+  return {start, end - start, 0, 0};
+}
+} // namespace native
diff --git a/native-runtime/address_space.h b/native-runtime/address_space.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..1677dfd60c878c2abf84d9dba1d2b7ffab38f2d5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/native-runtime/address_space.h
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+#pragma once
+#include <cstddef>
+#include <cstdint>
+#include <map>
+#include <stdexcept>
+#include <vector>
+namespace native {
+struct MemoryRegionInfo {
+  uint64_t address, size;
+  uint32_t state, permission;
+};
+class AddressSpace {
+public:
+  explicit AddressSpace(uint64_t limit = UINT64_C(1) << 39) : limit_(limit) {}
+  AddressSpace(const AddressSpace &) = delete;
+  AddressSpace &operator=(const AddressSpace &) = delete;
+  AddressSpace(AddressSpace &&) = delete;
+  AddressSpace &operator=(AddressSpace &&) = delete;
+  void map(uint64_t address, const std::vector<uint8_t> &bytes,
+           uint64_t memory_size, unsigned permission, uint32_t state = 5);
+  MemoryRegionInfo query(uint64_t address) const;
+  bool can_map(uint64_t address, uint64_t size,
+               uint32_t state = UINT32_MAX) const;
+  void reserve(uint64_t address, uint64_t size, uint32_t state);
+  MemoryRegionInfo reserved_range(uint32_t state) const;
+  uint64_t read(uint64_t address, unsigned size,
+                bool instruction = false) const;
+  void write(uint64_t address, unsigned size, uint64_t value);
+  void check(uint64_t address, unsigned size, unsigned permission) const;
+  uint64_t committed_bytes() const;
+  void set_physical_budget(uint64_t bytes) {
+    if (bytes < committed_bytes())
+      throw std::runtime_error("physical budget below committed memory");
+    physical_budget_ = bytes;
+  }
+  uint64_t physical_budget() const { return physical_budget_; }
+  size_t region_count() const { return regions_.size(); }
+  uint64_t address_limit() const { return limit_; }
+  void seal_code() { code_sealed_ = true; }
+  bool code_sealed() const { return code_sealed_; }
+
+private:
+  struct Region {
+    uint64_t address;
+    std::vector<uint8_t> bytes;
+    unsigned permission;
+    uint32_t state;
+  };
+  const Region &region(uint64_t address, unsigned permission) const;
+  std::map<uint64_t, Region> regions_;
+  std::map<uint64_t, MemoryRegionInfo> reservations_;
+  uint64_t limit_;
+  bool code_sealed_ = false;
+  uint64_t physical_budget_ = UINT64_MAX;
+};
+} // namespace native
diff --git a/native-runtime/boot.cpp b/native-runtime/boot.cpp
