diff --git a/native-runtime/nvn/README.md b/native-runtime/nvn/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..163e9625482fcddf9fa4e76a847df0c1ff7a5b82
--- /dev/null
+++ b/native-runtime/nvn/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,104 @@
+# Native NVN resource ownership
+
+`Resources` owns logical device, pool and buffer objects keyed by aligned guest
+integer addresses. It owns real Vulkan devices, buffer allocations and aliased
+views through `graphics/VulkanDevice`. No host pointer is written into guest
+state. Typed descriptions keep compatibility layouts and numeric flag decoding
+outside the component. No Core, kernel/process, Maxwell or service objects enter
+this interface.
+
+The initial supported pool mode is GPU cached with CPU cached or CPU no access.
+Virtual/physical pools and other cache modes fail explicitly. Backing storage
+and pool size require 4096-byte alignment; size is bounded to 16 MiB. Initial
+upload uses at most sixteen 1 MiB guest-read callbacks. Every explicit transfer
+is bounded to 1 MiB. Buffer views can have arbitrary in-range byte offsets and
+may alias the same pool. Distinct pools with overlapping guest backing are
+rejected because independent Vulkan allocations could diverge.
+
+CPU map returns the guest storage address (plus buffer offset), never a mapped
+host pointer. CPU-no-access pools reject map/flush/invalidate. Explicit flush
+reads guest bytes into temporary storage before updating/flushing Vulkan memory;
+a read failure leaves Vulkan bytes unchanged. Invalidate downloads/invalidate
+Vulkan bytes then invokes the guest write callback. A write failure is explicit
+and can retain partial guest effects according to the callback contract. CPU
+writes are not automatically coherent with Vulkan memory; callers must flush.
+
+`PoolGpuAddress`/`BufferGpuAddress` return real Vulkan buffer device addresses.
+`ResolveGpuAddress` resolves only a live owning pool and checked range.
+`Backend`, `View` and `Binding` borrow native objects for shader/command work;
+callers must complete GPU use before mutating or destroying them. Calls,
+callbacks and destruction are confined to the owner thread. Callbacks must be
+bounded, synchronous and non-reentrant. Live buffers block pool destruction;
+live pools block device destruction. Final owner teardown frees all resources.
+
+Build this directory standalone using the existing MSVC/Vulkan headers. The test
+submits a real `vkCmdCopyBuffer`, waits on a fence for at most five seconds and
+reads 64 copied bytes through guest-memory invalidation. It also checks real BDA,
+view aliasing, callback faults/partial writes, invalid ranges/modes/alignment,
+backing alias rejection, lifetime, key reuse and wrong-thread access. CTest has a
+30-second timeout. This is resource/GPU-copy evidence, not game rendering.
+
+Provenance: locally authored implementation, no LASRecomp code copied. The
+architectural reference was inspected at LASRecomp revision
+`99f783df21f60f48d512b95dd6536cb1ab48c2af` (MIT), `runtime/nvn/objects.c`.
+That title uses different builder offsets/default `0x9`, host pointers stored in
+guest objects and GPU-address-equals-CPU-address assumptions; none was adopted.
+It contains no verified public memory-pool flag enum. Numeric MK8D flag decoding
+therefore remains outside this typed API pending separately verified constants.
+No actual multi-block MK8D DeviceInitialize/MemoryPoolInitialize interception,
+presentation, draw submission, automatic guest coherence or standalone service
+closure is claimed by this component.
+
+## Bounded offscreen draw
+
+`draw.h` accepts caller-owned SPIR-V and an explicit scalar descriptor plan for
+set 0: uniform buffer ranges and combined RGBA8 2D sampled textures. It accepts
+location 0 float4 vertices with explicit stride, nonindexed or uint16/uint32
+indices, triangle lists/strips, bounded viewport/scissor and disabled/source-alpha
+blending. Target and texture dimensions are at most 2048; draw counts are at most
+1,048,576. Indices are checked against the vertex view before submission. No
+descriptor layout, shader input, texture contents or game arguments are inferred.
+
+Each call owns its temporary Vulkan image, upload/readback buffers, nearest/clamp
+samplers, descriptors, pipeline, command resources and fence. Texture uploads use
+explicit image transitions. A real draw is followed by image readback and a
+transfer-to-host barrier; the normal path waits up to five seconds for completion
+before returning owned RGBA8 bytes. Exception cleanup after a successful submit
+waits for device idle before destruction, so driver failure cleanup is not a
+hard real-time operation. Borrowed Resources buffers/device must remain alive,
+and all prior external queue uses must be complete. The API is owner-thread only.
+
+SPIR-V must already be valid Vulkan SPIR-V. Preflight checks structure, version,
+single main entry/stage, Logical GLSL450 model, enabled capability subset,
+32-bit scalar types, scalar UBO/combined nonarray 2D descriptor types and the
+explicit binding plan. Push constants, storage buffers, descriptor arrays,
+specialization constants, extensions and unimplemented capabilities fail
+explicitly. This targeted preflight does not replace a complete SPIR-V validator.
+Uniform ranges conservatively must cover reflected fixed scalar/vector/array/struct block
+members using explicit Offset/ArrayStride metadata. Unknown matrix/runtime
+layouts reject rather than allowing a shader to read beyond its bound range.
+This is the component's conservative rule, not a universal Vulkan requirement
+for unused block tails. Captured logical bytes must remain exact; no invented
+padding is used to satisfy it. A smaller binding requires separately verified
+active-access coverage before relaxing this rule.
+
+`native_nvn_draw_test` uses Sirit-authored fixture shaders: vertex location 0
+float4 and a fragment shader multiplying one UBO by samples from two textures.
+It checks known pixels for draw/draw-indexed, both index widths, topology,
+scissor and source-alpha blending, and rejects invalid metadata/state/indices.
+Those authored fixtures demonstrate component behavior only. They are not an
+actual MK8D draw, resource capture or evidence of native title rendering.
+
+Core Matrix/Shader/ImageQuery/SampledBuffer capabilities are accepted. Optional
+ImageGatherExtended is accepted only when `VulkanHandles` reports that the
+physical feature was queried and enabled on the actual device. Declaring a core
+capability does not widen the typed descriptor subset (buffer textures remain
+unsupported). The pure preflight entry point allows testing the disabled-feature
+case; GPU entry points always use the actual backend feature value.
+
+`CheckProgramPipeline` and `native_nvn_pipeline_check` create/destroy a real
+graphics pipeline using caller-supplied modules and an explicit per-stage binding
+plan. The CLI's `vertex:ubo:N`/`fragment:ubo:N`/`fragment:sampler:N` arguments must
+come from matching reflection evidence. It returns before command allocation or
+submission, binds no resource contents and produces no image. Pipeline acceptance
+does not establish actual game resource correctness or native title rendering.
diff --git a/native-runtime/nvn/buffer_init.cpp b/native-runtime/nvn/buffer_init.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..e393dc366b8fe4e1e649470281ed55991f563951
--- /dev/null
+++ b/native-runtime/nvn/buffer_init.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,144 @@
+#include "buffer_init.h"
+#include <array>
+#include <stdexcept>
+namespace native_nvn {
+namespace {
+bool Overlap(uint64_t a, uint64_t as, uint64_t b, uint64_t bs) {
+  return a <= b ? b - a < as : a - b < bs;
+}
+uint64_t Le(std::span<const std::byte> bytes) {
+  uint64_t value = 0;
+  for (size_t i = 0; i < bytes.size(); i++)
+    value |= uint64_t(bytes[i]) << (8 * i);
+  return value;
+}
+} // namespace
+BufferInitializer::BufferInitializer(Resources &resources,
+                                     BufferInitMemory memory)
+    : resources_(resources), memory_(memory),
+      owner_(std::this_thread::get_id()) {
+  if (!memory.probe || !memory.peek || !memory.read || !memory.write)
+    throw std::runtime_error("BufferInit callbacks required");
+}
+void BufferInitializer::CheckOwner() const {
+  if (owner_ != std::this_thread::get_id())
+    throw std::runtime_error("BufferInit owner thread required");
+}
+void BufferInitializer::RegisterPool(GuestAddress pool, GuestAddress device,
+                                     uint64_t size, size_t object_bytes) {
+  CheckOwner();
+  resources_.Backend(device);
+  const auto actual = resources_.ResolveGpuAddress(
+      device, resources_.PoolGpuAddress(pool), size);
+  if (actual.pool != pool || actual.offset)
+    throw std::runtime_error("Native pool association mismatch");
+  if (!pool || (pool & 7) || !size || object_bytes < 18 ||
+      object_bytes > 4096 || pools_.contains(pool))
+    throw std::runtime_error("Native pool registration invalid");
+  pools_.emplace(pool, OwnedPool{device, size, object_bytes});
+}
+void BufferInitializer::UnregisterPool(GuestAddress pool) {
+  CheckOwner();
+  if (!pools_.erase(pool))
+    throw std::runtime_error("Native pool not registered");
+}
+void BufferInitializer::Finalize(GuestAddress output) {
+  CheckOwner();
+  resources_.DestroyBuffer(output);
+}
+BufferInitResult BufferInitializer::Initialize(GuestAddress output,
+                                               GuestAddress builder) {
+  CheckOwner();
+  const BufferInitResult decline{BufferInitOutcome::Decline, 0},
+      fault{BufferInitOutcome::Fault, 0};
+  if (!output || (output & 7) || (builder & 7) || output > UINT64_MAX - 48 ||
+      builder > UINT64_MAX - 32 || Overlap(output, 48, builder, 32) ||
+      !memory_.probe(memory_.user, output, 48, true) ||
+      !memory_.probe(memory_.user, builder, 32, false))
+    return decline;
+  std::array<std::byte, 32> snapshot{};
+  if (!memory_.peek(memory_.user, builder, snapshot))
+    return decline;
+  const auto device = Le(std::span(snapshot).subspan(0, 8)),
+             pool = Le(std::span(snapshot).subspan(8, 8));
+  const auto offset = Le(std::span(snapshot).subspan(16, 8)),
+             size = Le(std::span(snapshot).subspan(24, 8));
+  const auto owner = pools_.find(pool);
+  if (owner == pools_.end() || owner->second.device != device ||
+      pool > UINT64_MAX - owner->second.object_bytes ||
+      Overlap(output, 48, pool, owner->second.object_bytes) ||
+      !memory_.probe(memory_.user, pool + 17, 1, false))
+    return decline;
+  try {
+    const auto actual = resources_.ResolveGpuAddress(
+        device, resources_.PoolGpuAddress(pool), owner->second.size);
+    if (actual.pool != pool || actual.offset)
+      return decline;
+  } catch (const std::runtime_error &) {
+    return decline;
+  }
+  bool live_output = false;
+  try {
+    resources_.Binding(output);
+    live_output = true;
+  } catch (const std::runtime_error &) {
+  }
+  try {
+    resources_.PoolGpuAddress(output);
+    live_output = true;
+  } catch (const std::runtime_error &) {
+  }
+  try {
+    resources_.Backend(output);
+    live_output = true;
+  } catch (const std::runtime_error &) {
+  }
+  if (live_output)
+    return decline;
+  std::array<std::byte, 1> flag{};
+  if (!memory_.peek(memory_.user, pool + 17, flag))
+    return decline;
+  const bool failure = (uint8_t(flag[0]) & 1) != 0;
+  if (!failure && (!size || offset > owner->second.size ||
+                   size > owner->second.size - offset))
+    return decline;
+  bool created = false;
+  if (!failure) {
+    try {
+      resources_.CreateBuffer(output, {device, pool, offset, size});
+      created = true;
+    } catch (const std::runtime_error &) {
+      return decline;
+    }
+  }
+  auto fail = [&] {
+    if (created)
+      resources_.DestroyBuffer(output);
+    return fault;
+  };
+  std::array<std::byte, 16> zero{};
+  for (auto at : {32u, 16u, 0u})
+    if (!memory_.write(memory_.user, output + at, zero))
+      return fail();
+  std::array<std::byte, 8> value{};
+  if (!memory_.read(memory_.user, builder + 8, value))
+    return fail();
+  if (Le(value) != pool)
+    return fail();
+  std::array<std::byte, 1> actual_flag{};
+  if (!memory_.read(memory_.user, pool + 17, actual_flag) ||
+      actual_flag != flag)
+    return fail();
+  if (failure)
+    return {BufferInitOutcome::Failure, 0};
+  const uint64_t expected[] = {device, pool, offset, size};
+  for (size_t i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
+    if (!memory_.read(memory_.user, builder + i * 8, value) ||
+        Le(value) != expected[i])
+      return fail();
+    if (!memory_.write(memory_.user, output + 8 + i * 8, value))
+      return fail();
+  }
+  return {BufferInitOutcome::Success, 1};
+}
+} // namespace native_nvn
