diff --git a/tests/native_entry/README.md b/tests/native_entry/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..9f7e4f8b66f3f183bbaca614626a8fe46cb1c458
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/native_entry/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# Guarded native entry fixture
+
+Run `python run.py --build <isolated-build-directory>` in a compiler-enabled shell.
+This synthetic query has a known complete two-instruction returning body. It is
+not an NVN resolver implementation or a claim of graphics coverage.
+
+The generator requires an explicit matching build identity, full discovered block
+bytes and RET X30. Partial, changed and duplicate descriptors fail generation.
+Unknown identity preserves the original export byte for byte. Runtime bindings
+negotiate exact revision, size and bounded-return capability; missing or invalid
+bindings preserve the original guarded instructions. Installing/removing a binding
+requires all guest threads quiescent. Binding/user storage remains immutable and
+alive while guest threads run; callbacks must support independent guest contexts.
+
+Tests compare full GuestContext state, memory reads, interior entry, local slice,
+returned guest-address indirect route, host lookup, budgets, halt/SVC and invalid
+binding fallback. Each skipped word is mutated in a separate strict-guard child.
+The caller is also exported as a separate generated module and linked against
+the same runtime. Its guest-address indirect transfer reaches the native query
+exactly once through module B's lookup without altering the dispatch budget.
+
+The fixture enables FM1/GG1. Separate children first exercise a native hit and a
+cached-generation hit, then publish a new generation before changed code,
+remapped code, unmapped/protected code or a replaced page table. Every invalid
+case rejects before a second callback or data access. These fixtures model the
+host's required generation publication; they do not prove that a particular
+host's mapping/protection notification code publishes it correctly.
+Multi-block substitution is deliberately unsupported until all skipped ranges can
+be guarded. No title-specific addresses are selected by this fixture.
